So, as I understand your overall design you're talking about a unifying
application framework with some fancy (or simplistic depending on your POV)
recursion to take care of chaining things together.

 

Forgive me for sounding cynical, but how is that different from .NET (and
its IL)?  I suppose the positivist translation would be "what problems does
this system address?"

 

